sequenceDiagram
    participant Admin as Gate Admin
    participant Gate as eFTI Gate (eu-ee31)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Admin->>+Gate: POST /api/v1/authorities
    Note over Admin,Gate: Authorization: Bearer {TARA-JWT, role=ADMIN}<br/>Body: {"id":"aut-politsei-001","name":"Police and Border Guard Board","countryCode":"EE","subsets":["EU07","EU01"]}

    Gate->>Gate: Validate JWT (signature, exp, iss, aud);<br/>require resource_access.efti-gate.roles ∋ ADMIN

    Gate->>+DB: INSERT INTO authorities (id, name, country_code, subsets, created_by, created_at)<br/>VALUES ('aut-politsei-001', 'Police and Border Guard Board', 'EE', '{EU07,EU01}', $admin_uid, NOW())
    DB-->>-Gate: OK (new row; latest row for this id wins)

    Gate-->>Admin: 201 Created\n{"id":"aut-politsei-001","name":"Police and Border Guard Board","countryCode":"EE","subsets":["EU07","EU01"]}

    Note over Admin: Authority registered with allowed subsets.<br/>Now create authority users.

    Admin->>+Gate: POST /api/v1/users
    Note over Admin,Gate: Body: {"name":"Officer Jaan Tamm","email":"jaan.tamm@politsei.ee","roles":{"AUTHORITY":["aut-politsei-001"]},"subsets":["EU07"]}<br/>(no secret — primary auth is TARA-issued JWT)

    Gate->>Gate: Validate user.subsets ⊆ authority.subsets:<br/>["EU07"] ⊆ ["EU07","EU01"] → OK

    Gate->>+DB: INSERT INTO users (id, name, email, roles, subsets, secret_hash, created_by, created_at)<br/>VALUES (uuid_generate_v4(), 'Officer Jaan Tamm', 'jaan.tamm@politsei.ee',<br/>'{"AUTHORITY":["aut-politsei-001"]}', '{EU07}', NULL, $admin_uid, NOW())
    DB-->>-Gate: row inserted; user.id="d2e3f4a5-..."

    Gate-->>-Admin: 201 Created\n{"id":"d2e3f4a5-...","name":"Officer Jaan Tamm","email":"jaan.tamm@politsei.ee","roles":{"AUTHORITY":["aut-politsei-001"]},"subsets":["EU07"]}

    Note over Admin: Authority user created with EU07 subset only.<br/>User authenticates via TARA OIDC; the gate's `users.id`<br/>is matched on first login by the TARA `sub` claim<br/>(Estonian PIC) against `users.email` (or a separate<br/>`users.tara_sub` column in a future migration).

    alt Invalid subsets (user requests more than authority allows)
        Admin->>Gate: POST /api/v1/users (subsets=["EU01","EU03"], authority subsets=["EU07","EU01"])
        Gate->>Gate: Validate: ["EU01","EU03"] ⊄ ["EU07","EU01"] → fails
        Gate-->>Admin: 400 Bad Request\n{"code":"BAD_REQUEST_GENERAL","detail":"User subsets must be a subset of the authority's subsets."}
    end
